NOTE ON SCOPE

This MIT license covers the CODE in this repository: everything under src/
and tests/.

The prose in docs/ is licensed separately under CC BY 4.0. See docs/LICENSE.
The split is deliberate: the code should be reusable without friction, and
the written analysis should stay attributable, because attribution is what
lets a reader trace a claim back to the sample it came from. Several numbers
in that text are illustrative measurements from three matches, not
constants, and stripping them from their source is how illustrative numbers
become folklore.
